BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intro to Wheel Throwing with Naomi & Jack — Sebastopol Center Fo
 r the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20260521T000000
DTEND:20260522T000000
UID:c3beddb404864f1b97bd80bf83590ab9@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Out of Stock\n      \n    \n\n\n\n\n\nIntro to Wheel Throwing 
 with Naomi & Jack\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $295.00\n      
   \n      \n    \n  \n\nThursdays\, May 21 -June 25\, 2026\; 2-5pm (6 week
 s)$250 + $45 Clay Fee (max 8 students)This course is designed for students
  who are new to the potter’s wheel and eager to discover the fundamental
 s of wheel throwing. With an emphasis on core technique\, each session bui
 lds a solid foundation in the essential skills of centering\, opening\, pu
 lling up walls\, trimming and glazing — the building blocks that every p
 otter returns to again and again.Each class begins with a demonstration fo
 cused on one or more of these foundational techniques\, giving students a 
 clear picture of the process before getting their hands in the clay. From 
 there\, students work at their own wheels with plenty of time to practice\
 , explore and develop their feel for the material. The goal is for each pe
 rson to leave the course being able to make a thrown piece — a bowl\, a 
 mug\, a vase — that is genuinely their own\, shaped by their emerging sk
 ills and their personal sense of what they love about pottery.With two tea
 chers in the room\, there is ample opportunity for individual attention an
 d hands-on guidance at every stage of the process. At the same time\, ther
 e is real joy in learning alongside others — watching a classmate pull u
 p a wall for the first time\, or seeing a finished glaze come out of the k
 iln — and that shared experience is very much a part of what makes this 
 class special.No prior experience is necessary. All you need is curiosity 
 and a willingness to get a little muddy.About the Instructors: Naomi Fuchs
  brings a deep love of clay and a genuine passion for sharing the experien
 ce with others to everything she does in the clay room. She believes that 
 each pot is an opportunity to learn — about the nature of clay\, and abo
 ut yourself. Naomi has been throwing on the wheel for four years\, and in 
 that time the practice has become a grounding\, peaceful and creative part
  of her life that has deepened her connection to art and making. Her warm\
 , encouraging approach creates a space where beginners feel supported as t
 hey find their footing at the wheel and begin to discover what clay can do
  in their hands.In just one year\, pottery has become one of Jack Harrison
 ’s passions—a craft that continues to humble him\, calm him\, and insp
 ire him as he shapes both the clay and his own journey. Throwing vases is 
 what he does most\, but he is experienced in all areas of the wheel. Shari
 ng his passion with others in the studio has allowed him to become part of
  a community that supports and challenges each other. As a mellow\, focuse
 d individual\, beginners will find comfort in learning from him.\n\n\n\n\n
 \n          \n            \n              \n                Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/intro-to-wheel-throwing-with-
 naomi-jack
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
