BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jizo Peace Project — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20260605T000000
DTEND:20260606T000000
UID:19df54a41591aabcc32627e09b5c2bfd@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Jizo Peace Project: Clay Gathering for Remembrance and Peace\,
  June\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $10.00\n        \n      \n 
    \n  \n\nFriday\, June 5\, 2026\; 1:30 – 4:00pmDue to limited capacity
 \, we are asking for a suggested donation of $10 to confirm your attendanc
 e. Bring a copy of your receipt at check-in to Painting/Drawing Studio adj
 acent to Ceramics StudioJoin us for a monthly\, heart-centered gathering w
 here we come together to create Jizo guardians out of clay—symbols of co
 mpassion\, protection\, and peace. Rooted in the Buddhist tradition and ec
 hoed across many cultures\, Jizo figures traditionally honor children and 
 all who have passed\, those in transition\, and those in distress.This ong
 oing project is dedicated to remembering those lost to war\, with a specia
 l focus now on the approximately 19\,000 children who have perished in Isr
 ael and Gaza in recent years. Through the simple\, meditative act of worki
 ng with clay\, we create benevolent beings that will become part of public
  exhibits and peace sites\, offering spaces for reflection\, mourning\, an
 d hope. Our gatherings conclude with a gentle ritual to honor the lives of
  these children.Located in the Painting & Drawing Room. The gathering is o
 pen to ages 12 - adult\, and no prior clay experience is necessary—all c
 lay and basic materials are supplied. Registration is required to particip
 ate.Donations are welcome to help cover materials and expenses. More than 
 a class\, this is a shared space of warmth and care—an opportunity to te
 nd to our own hearts while taking part in love in action.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \
